  "content": {
    "id": "p49-q22-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "22",
    "prompt": "Five years ago I was 5 times as old as my son.\nIn 8 years’ time I will be 3 times as old as my son.\nHow old am I today?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "70 years old.",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be my current age and $y$ be my son’s current age, in years.\n$$\\begin{align*}x-5 &= 5(y-5) \\qquad (1)\\\\x+8 &= 3(y+8) \\qquad (2)\\end{align*}$$\nRearrange (1) and substitute into (2):\n$$\\begin{align*}x-5 &= 5y-25\\\\x &= 5y-20\\\\5y-20+8 &= 3(y+8)\\\\5y-12 &= 3y+24\\\\2y &= 36\\\\y &= 18\\\\x &= 5(18)-20\\\\x &= 70\\end{align*}$$\nI am 70 years old today.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 85
  },
